  "description": "Structural rank probe of the A^λ_{μν}(I) supply matrix at A=3 (split 3+6).  For each λ, builds the full M matrix from the test panel and computes the SVD spectrum.  Rank is the count of singular values above the relative threshold 1e-12 · sv[0]; the drop ratio between sv[rank-1] and sv[rank] establishes whether the null directions are EXACT zeros (drop ≫ 1e6) or panel-limited approximations.  Empirical finding: rank is structurally less than ambient n_unknowns for all multi-block λ — establishing item 4 (symmetry reductions) is required for full A=4 closure.",
